//
// PROBE: `#.`, which runs a lambda over the value an object wraps, taking the
// object from the workbench.
//
// `#` pulls the lambda, then the object, unwraps the object and runs the
// lambda with `!` (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/oop/object_execute.rs:10-45).
// `#.` takes the object from the workbench instead, and guards a stack depth
// of one rather than two (:43-45). The object is built as the corpus's own
// `object_execute.bund` builds it.
//
"probe: #. takes the object from the workbench" println
41 :Integer object .
{ 1 + } #.
"Answer is {A}" format println
